// CRAMER - Cramer's rule for AX=B, A square, B a column.
// x_i = det(A_i)/det(A), A_i = A with column i replaced by B.
// Out: [C] = solution
ClrHome
Disp "CRAMER RULE AX=B"
dim([A])→ʟZD
If ʟZD(1)≠ʟZD(2):Then
Disp "A MUST BE SQUARE"
Return
End
ʟZD(1)→G
det([A])→O
If abs(O-round(O,0))<1ᴇ⁻9*max(1,abs(O))
round(O,0)→O
If abs(O)<1ᴇ⁻10:Then
Disp "DET(A)=0","CRAMER NOT APPLICABLE"
Return
End
Disp "DET(A) ="
Pause O►Frac
{G,1}→dim([C])
For(I,1,G)
[A]→[H]
For(K,1,G)
[B](K,1)→[H](K,I)
End
det([H])→X
If abs(X-round(X,0))<1ᴇ⁻9*max(1,abs(X))
round(X,0)→X
X/O→[C](I,1)
ClrHome
Disp "DET(A"+sub("123456789",I,1)+") ="
Disp X►Frac
Disp "X"+sub("123456789",I,1)+" ="
Pause (X/O)►Frac
End
ClrHome
Disp "SOLUTION X = [C]"
Pause [C]►Frac
